==English==

===Etymology===
{{suffix|strike|er}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# An individual who is [[on strike]].
# Someone or something that hits someone or something else.
## A [[blacksmith]]'s assistant who wields the [[sledgehammer]].
# {{soccer}} One of the players on a team in [[football]] ([[soccer]]) in the row nearest to the opposing team's [[goal]], who are therefore principally responsible for [[scoring]] goals.
#*{{quote-news
|year=2011
|date=September 28
|author=Tom Rostance
|title=Arsenal   2 - 1   Olympiakos
|work=BBC Sport
|url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/14998317.stm
|page=
|passage=Olympiakos had barely been in the Arsenal half but should have levelled in the 14th minute. A low corner was not dealt with and the ball fell to the feet of '''striker''' Rafik Djebbour, who saw his close-range effort brilliantly cleared from the goalline by Arteta.}}
#{{baseball|slang|1800s}} The [[batter]].
#{{cricket}} The [[batsman]] who is currently facing the [[bowler]] and defending his [[wicket]].
# {{obsolete}} A [[harpoon]].
# {{obsolete}} A [[harpooner]].
#: ''Wherever we come to an anchor, we always send out our '''strikers''', and put out hooks and lines overboard, to try fish.'' &mdash; Dampier.
# {{obsolete}} A [[wencher]]; a [[lewd]] [[man]].
#: {{rfquotek|Massinger}}
# {{obsolete|politics}} A [[blackmailer]] in [[politics]].
# {{obsolete|politics}} One whose [[political]] [[influence]] can be [[buy|bought]].

